      "text": "STEVE BRINGS THE NEWS",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "start": 22.8,
      "end": 27.88,
      "text": "Steve Chapman turned from Chapel Street into the quieter thoroughfare, metaphorically speaking,",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "start": 27.88,
      "end": 32.86,
      "text": "two wheels, bounded up the steps of the fourth house in the row, took the first flight of",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "start": 32.86,
      "end": 38.219997,
      "text": "stairs on high, raced along the corridor, skidded a bit at the last portal on the right,",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "start": 38.34,
      "end": 43.739998,
      "text": "and finally, setting all brakes, came to a standstill in the center of the floor, while",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "start": 43.739998,
      "end": 48.42,
      "text": "as the door swung back against the wall, every picture in the study jarred askew.",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "start": 49.34,
      "end": 51.64,
      "text": "War's begun, he announced breathlessly.",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "start": 52.14,
      "end": 53.6,
      "text": "President Wilson has signed.",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "start": 54,
      "end": 55.32,
      "text": "We're in it at last, Joe.",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "start": 55.32,
      "end": 60,
      "text": "Joe Ingersoll regarded his roommate calmly across the desk...",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "start": 60,
      "end": 62.26,
      "text": "one hand holding open the book he had been studying.",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "start": 62.98,
      "end": 65.96,
      "text": "But why wreck the premises? he asked mildly.",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "start": 66.44,
      "end": 68.94,
      "text": "What do you think you are, the German army in Belgium?",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "start": 70.16,
      "end": 72.98,
      "text": "Steve, subsiding against the back of the Morris chair,",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "start": 73.42,
      "end": 76.359999,
      "text": "strove to regain his breath and wither the other with a glance,",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "start": 76.68,
      "end": 78.72,
      "text": "a not particularly successful effort.",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "start": 79.56,
      "end": 81.3,
      "text": "You make me tired, he declared.",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "start": 81.69999899999999,
      "end": 83.84,
      "text": "Where's your patriotism, you block of wood?",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "start": 83.84,
      "end": 87.56,
      "text": "I nearly break my neck to get the joyful news to you,",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "start": 87.56,
      "end": 90.439999,
      "text": "and you sit there like... like...",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "start": 90.439999,
      "end": 91.74,
      "text": "Calm yourself, Stephen.",
      "check": false
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "start": 92.28,
      "end": 93.52000000000001,
      "text": "I've known it for at least...",
      "check": false
    }
